  "definition": "Carotid stenosis is a narrowing of part of the carotid arteries, usually caused by buildup of atherosclerotic plaque. The narrowed area can develop clots or release platelet or cholesterol material that may lead to a transient ischemic attack, stroke, or temporary blindness.",
